<!--
  Whole-body-controller stage plugins (issue #6, M2.1).

  base_class_type: StagePlugin<WBCInterface<JointTorqueVelocityPositionCommands>>
    (mit_controller/stage_plugin.hpp + mit_controller/wbc_interface.hpp
     + mit_controller/joint_commands.hpp)

  WBCInterface is still a class template (gap G8, issue #13), so there is no single
  StagePlugin<WBCInterface> base — only per-command-type instantiations. For the M2
  Go2 product path the base is the JointTorqueVelocityPositionCommands instantiation
  (doc/modularity/plugin_lifecycle.md §6). When #13 (M3.2) de-templates the
  interface, THIS FILE is the one that gets reworked — the other stage XML files are
  unaffected, which is why the WBC declaration is isolated here.

  Stock wrappers filled in by M2.3 (issue #8): wbc_arc_opt and inverse_dynamics, in
  src/plugins/wbc_plugins.cpp, both built into libwbc_plugins. Because WBCInterface
  is a template, the two register under two different base_class_types in the same
  library: wbc_arc_opt under the JointTorqueVelocityPositionCommands instantiation
  (stage_plugin_bases::kWBC, the Go2 path) and inverse_dynamics under the
  CartesianCommands instantiation (stage_plugin_bases::kWBCCartesian, the ULab/ikin
  path). #13 (M3.2) collapses these into one once the interface is de-templated.

  The '<' in base_class_type is XML-escaped as &lt;/&gt; (stage_loading.md §5).
  The `name` (type: key) vocabulary is owned by M2.5 (#10); this file is
  naming-agnostic per doc/modularity/plugin_lifecycle.md.
-->
<class_libraries>
  <library path="libwbc_plugins">
    <class name="wbc_arc_opt"
           type="stock_plugins::WbcArcOptPlugin"
           base_class_type="StagePlugin&lt;WBCInterface&lt;JointTorqueVelocityPositionCommands&gt;&gt;">
      <description>ARC-OPT task-space inverse dynamics WBC producing joint torque/velocity/position
        commands (WBCArcOPT), the Go2 path.</description>
    </class>
    <class name="inverse_dynamics"
           type="stock_plugins::InverseDynamicsPlugin"
           base_class_type="StagePlugin&lt;WBCInterface&lt;CartesianCommands&gt;&gt;">
      <description>Inverse-dynamics WBC producing Cartesian foot commands (InverseDynamics), the
        ULab/ikin path.</description>
    </class>
  </library>
</class_libraries>
